# Fleet keeper pass, seat A (fleet-ops#10204). Nish, 2026-10-24: "two claude
# accounts exist on the vps solely to fix such failures, inexcusable. please make
# it so that they keep a check on everything". This unit is one of the two seats;
# fleet-keeper-b.service is the other, 30 minutes later, on the second login.
#
# What runs: prompts/fleet-keeper.md through `claude -p`, twice an hour, with the
# seat's own gh login (nish3451, ~/.config/gh/hosts.yml) and no App token. The
# keeper dispatches work with `gh workflow run agent-dispatch.yml`, which needs
# Actions write, and the nishfleet-worker App token of
# fleet-worker-github-token@.service has no Workflows permission - so this unit
# uses the runner user's own login the way fleet-pr-sweep@.service and
# agent-dispatch.yml's orchestrate job already do. The packet's own "Never" list
# is the control on that grant: no approval, no coordinator-approval, no owner
# key, no secret rotation.
#
# No OnFailure= on this unit, on purpose. fleet-unit-failed@.service starts this
# unit, so pointing this unit back at it would be a failure loop that pages and
# starts passes forever. A pass that dies is caught two ways instead: the
# ExecStopPost dead-man below fails the unit, which leaves it listed for the
# other seat's step 3, and the other seat's own timer runs 30 minutes later.
#
# The environment is stripped. A desktop session leaked its CLAUDE_* and
# ANTHROPIC_* variables into the user manager on 2026-10-24, so every background
# unit inherited them: a leaked ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL sends this seat's calls to the
# wrong provider, a leaked CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR points the seat at the other login,
# and a leaked GH_TOKEN swaps the login for an App token that cannot dispatch.
# UnsetEnvironment= is applied as the last step, so it also undoes Environment=;
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is therefore unset here and re-added on the command line by
# the seat that needs it (fleet-keeper-b.service), never through Environment=.
#
# One date: ExecStart writes the deliverable path into the runtime directory
# once, so a pass that crosses midnight IST names its report and its dead-man
# with the same string.
#
# %%, $$: systemd expands % and $ itself before any shell runs, so every shell $
# is written $$ and every shell % is written %% (ci.yml gate fleet-ops#8382).
#
# Switch off: systemctl --user disable --now fleet-keeper-a.timer
# Delete: README "Fleet keeper" lists the files.
[Unit]
Description=Fleet keeper pass, seat A, default login (fleet-ops#10204)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
RuntimeDirectory=fleet-keeper-a
RuntimeDirectoryMode=0700
WorkingDirectory=%h/workspaces
# 30 min is the cap for a pass. Type=oneshot runs its ExecStart in the start phase,
# so RuntimeMaxSec= is ignored for this shape and TimeoutStartSec= is the directive
# that bounds it, the same pairing retro-weekly.service uses. The packet's own cap
# is 25 min, so a pass that reaches 30 min is one that is stuck.
TimeoutStartSec=30min
UMask=0077
Environment=TZ=Asia/Kolkata
Environment=LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
Environment=FLEET_TASK_ID=fleet-keeper-a
Environment=FLEET_KEEPER_REPO=%h/workspaces/tooling/fleet-ops-deploy-clone
UnsetEnvironment=ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL ANTHROPIC_CUSTOM_HEADERS ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL ANTHROPIC_MODEL ANTHROPIC_SMALL_FAST_MODEL CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR CLAUDE_CODE_ENTRYPOINT CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_TURNS CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN CLAUDE_CODE_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK CLAUDE_CODE_USE_FOUNDRY CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR GH_TOKEN GITHUB_TOKEN MAX_THINKING_TOKENS
# The deliverable path is written once, here, and read by the dead-man below.
# The user manager's default UMask is 0002, so the report of a pass (findings,
# unit names, session text) would otherwise be group and world readable.
ExecStart=/bin/sh -c 'd=$$(date +%%F); export DELIVERABLE=%h/workspaces/docs/proof/$$d-pi-packets/keeper-a.md; mkdir -p "$$(dirname "$$DELIVERABLE")"; printf %%s "$$DELIVERABLE" > "$$RUNTIME_DIRECTORY/deliverable"; exec %h/.local/bin/claude -p --permission-mode dontAsk < "$$FLEET_KEEPER_REPO/prompts/fleet-keeper.md"'
# `claude -p` exits 0 on a model refusal, so the report on disk is the only
# proof the pass ran. A pass that wrote nothing fails the unit here.
ExecStopPost=/bin/sh -c 'test -s "$$(cat "$$RUNTIME_DIRECTORY/deliverable" 2>/dev/null)" || { echo "fleet-keeper-a: the pass wrote no deliverable" >&2; exit 1; }'
